          <p>{proof.body}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="parents">Talking to your parents when you are not sure</h2>

  <p>
    Parents often hear "I am confused" as "I have no plan". Change what they hear by showing them the plan for finding the answer.
  </p>

  <div class="split-grid">
    <div class="split-card split-card--grow">
      <div class="split-card__label">Try saying</div>
      <ul>
        <li>"I have narrowed it to two routes, and here is what each keeps open."</li>
        <li>"I want to test both before the admission date. Can we agree on a review day?"</li>
        <li>"Here is my backup if the first choice does not work."</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="split-card split-card--grow">
      <div class="split-card__label">Try to avoid</div>
      <ul>
        <li>"I do not know and I do not care."</li>
        <li>"All my friends are doing it."</li>
        <li>"You never listen to me."</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p>
    Parents: ask your child what they have tried and can show you before you ask which stream sounds safe. Comparing them with cousins adds fear and no facts, and a large coaching fee should be judged against the work it leads to, not the name on the building.
  </p>

  <h2 id="low-marks">If your marks are low or the usual path feels closed</h2>

  <p>
    A low mark is a data point, not a verdict. It narrows some doors and leaves others fully open.
  </p>

  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--teal">
    <p><strong>Try first</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Ask the school for its minimum marks for each group, in writing. The rule is set by the school or the state.</li>
      <li>Ask your board whether you can improve a score. CBSE now offers an optional second Class 10 exam, held from 15 to 21 May 2026 for up to three subjects, with the better score counted. Read the CBSE notice for your own year before you rely on it.</li>
      <li>Look at open school, diploma and ITI as real routes, each with its own next step.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="honest-take">
    <p class="honest-take__label">Do not do</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Pay a seat fee or a "guaranteed admission" fee to an agent.</li>
      <li>Choose a group only because a friend got into it.</li>
      <li>Pick a route to hide your marks from your family. Show them the plan instead.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <p>
    See <a href="/blog/college-degrees/courses-for-weak-students-after-10th-india/">courses for students with low marks after 10th</a> and <a href="/blog/career-guidance/how-to-choose-a-career-as-a-teenager/">how to choose a career as a teenager</a> for the next step.
  </p>

  <h2 id="money">Money check before you pay</h2>

  <p>
    Our strongest suggestion: keep any course or coaching fee near a tenth of the family's total education budget, and treat spending above roughly a fifth as a caution that needs course-specific evidence. This does not apply to very cheap online learning. Free YouTube lessons and low-priced courses on sites like Udemy or Coursera need little budget care, and the same course sold as a university certificate can cost 30 to 100 times more.
  </p>

  <p>
    An illustration, not a real fee: if the family sets aside Rs 6 lakh for your whole education, a tenth is Rs 60,000 for the biggest single item and a fifth is Rs 1.2 lakh. The rest should still fund the later degree, a laptop, books and a reserve.
  </p>

  <p>
    General information, not financial advice; get fee and refund terms in writing. Apply only on the official website of a school, board or institute, and do not pay an agent who promises a seat.
  </p>

  <h2 id="portfolio">Build a high-income skill portfolio beside your route, not instead of it</h2>

  <p>
    Marks open the first door. A high-income skill portfolio, which means the right skill mix for you, proof of work, clear communication and a fit with how you like to work, builds the choices that come after it.
  </p>

  <div class="ladder">
    {skillSteps.map((step, i) => (
      <div class="ladder-step">
        <div class="ladder-step__num">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</div>
        <div>
          <div class="ladder-step__title">{step.title}</div>
          <p>{step.body}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <div class="honest-take honest-take--teal">
    <p class="honest-take__label">The part that can scale</p>
    <p>
      A skill that other people value, such as design, video editing, coding or teaching a subject, is the one thing you can build beside any route that can grow past a single job. Later, when you are older and a parent agrees, you can set your own price, serve more people and bring in helpers, which a fixed salary cannot do.
    </p>
    <p>
      At 15, the goal is finished samples and feedback, not income. Keep school first.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="heavier">When it feels heavier than confusion</h2>

  <div class="honest-take">
    <p class="honest-take__label">Please read this</p>
    <p>
      If you feel hopeless, cannot sleep or eat, or keep thinking you have ruined your life over one choice, tell a trusted adult today. You can also call Tele-MANAS, the government's free helpline, on 14416 or 1800-89-14416, open 24 hours a day and in more than 20 languages (PIB, 24 April 2023).
    </p>
    <p>
      Not medical advice; talk to a doctor or counsellor.
    </p>
  </div>

