  <h2 id="next-step">What to do next</h2>

  <p>
    Start now: cut your list to two routes and pick one sample task for each. Then book one conversation with a person who lives each route, and write your decision note with a review date.
  </p>

  <p><strong>Try it now:</strong> <a href="/services/assessments/confused-about-career-after-10th-test/">Take the free Confused About Career After 10th test</a> for a scored breakdown of what is holding you back: knowing yourself, knowing the options, family pressure or indecision.</p>

  <p>
    If you are still stuck after that, the problem is usually missing information, not missing ability. Continuous guidance from <a href="/services/career-counselling-and-career-guidance/">Future Career School</a> helps you and your family compare routes honestly and make the decisions that unlock high income opportunities, with a plan that keeps working after Class 12. Message us on WhatsApp from that page to start.
  </p>

